  "final_message": "I have launched `npm test` and will wait for it to complete.\nI am waiting for the test suite execution to finish.\nI have initiated the test run and am waiting for the execution to finish.\nI am waiting for `npm test` to finish.\nI am waiting for the build and test process to complete.\nI am waiting for the git log search to complete.\nI am checking git history for previous deprecations.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model due to architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/GEMINI.md).\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly\n\n1. **ARCH-4 Compliance**:\n   > `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n   Removing `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) in [src/core/events.ts](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts) is a breaking change for downstream consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Under ARCH-4, changes to published events must be strictly additive.\n2. **Order Model Dependency**:\n   Because [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) must continue to include `channel` for downstream compatibility via [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59), the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model in [src/core/order.ts](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts) must retain the field as well.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\nTo retire this field properly:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29).\n2. Announce deprecation and coordinate with the owning teams for `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` to remove their dependencies.\n3. Once all consumers have deployed updates and no longer reference the field, complete the deprecation lifecycle and remove the field in a subsequent schema version.\n",
